  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A ball of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> and radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span> can be modelled as a thin spherical shell with moment of inertia <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I = \\frac{2}{3}MR^{2}\"></span>, where <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> is the mass and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span> is the radius of the ball. When the ball is kicked, it rolls on a horizontal surface without slipping, with angular velocity <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\omega\"></span> and linear speed <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the rotational kinetic energy of the ball?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{3}Mv^{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2}{3}Mv^{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{3}M\\omega^{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2}{3}M\\omega^{2}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
